From 74e980ae79d988b90eaacc46bf781b7a7a16afa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:14:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): ribbon tab and caption rows get their own height;
 glyphs white

Commit 37e7594ec gave the ribbon tab row and caption row no space of
their own and painted the glyphs in a steel blue ink. The tab text ran
into the button labels, the captions touched the labels above them and
the caption row met the bottom edge. The ribbon now has a tab row, a
cell row, a caption row and a bottom gap (88 px at default tokens). The
dark theme glyphs are white again. The light theme keeps dark ink.

The machine page test harnesses are raised to the app default height
(800 px): the taller ribbon moves the page's button row below 720 px.

Fixes #1994
Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
